WinRAR or WinZip should do the job.  In winzip, when you feed it a .tgz
file, it examines it, finds it contains a single .tar file, and asks you
if you want to unpack that.  I imagine WinRAR can do something similar,
though as far as I'm concerned, RARlab GmbH can, and indeed should, go
running with scissors.  (This isn't an advocacy group, so I'll leave it
at that.)

-xvf == eXtract Verbosely from File ; the following argument specifies
the filename.
